  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Seema Sarkar vs The State Of Telangana on 10 March, 2022",
    "facts": "However, the detention order also refers to the crime registered in the year 2018 alleging similar offences. It appears, in pursuant to the crime registered on 05.07.2018, the detenu was detained vide order of detention dated 20.09.2018. The said detention order was [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court in W.P.No.33705 of 2018.",
    "arguments": "5. Learned counsel for the petitioner contends that the order of detention reads as if the detenu is indulging in similar crimes continuously since the year 2018, whereas, he was involved in one crime in the year 2018 and this is the second crime. She would submit that this also shows total non-application of mind in dealing with the issue of preventively detaining a person offending his right to life and liberty. Learned counsel further submits that on 26.11.2021 the criminal Court granted bail by imposing certain conditions. The first condition is that the accused should execute personal bond for Rs.10,000/- with two sureties each and the second condition that he should not leave Hyderabad city, without prior permission of the jurisdictional Magistrate. She therefore submits that the conditions imposed in the bail order sufficiently safeguard the interest of the prosecution. According to learned counsel, the facts of the case do not warrant resorting to extreme measure of preventive detention. By referring to various decisions, she submits that considering the past record is also erroneous and vitiates the order of detention on that ground 6. Having satisfied with the prima-facie issue of detaining the detenu by referring to solitary crime registered in the year 2018 we are not going into the other contentions urged by learned counsel for the petitioner. 7. Suffice to note that though, the detenu was detained earlier on account of involvement in similar crime, but the said order of detention was [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. Learned counsel for the petitioner contends that the order of detention reads as if the detenu is indulging in similar crimes continuously since the year 2018, whereas, he was involved in one crime in the year 2018 and this is the second crime. She would submit that this also shows total non-application of mind in dealing with the issue of preventively detaining a person offending his right to life and liberty. Learned counsel further submits that on 26.11.2021 the criminal Court granted bail by imposing certain conditions. The first condition is that the accused should execute personal bond for Rs.10,000/- with two sureties each and the second condition that he should not leave Hyderabad city, without prior permission of the jurisdictional Magistrate. She therefore submits that the conditions imposed in the bail order sufficiently safeguard the interest of the prosecution.",
    "respondent_arguments": "According to learned counsel, the facts of the case do not warrant resorting to extreme measure of preventive detention. By referring to various decisions, she submits that considering the past record is also erroneous and vitiates the order of detention on that ground 6. Having satisfied with the prima-facie issue of detaining the detenu by referring to solitary crime registered in the year 2018 we are not going into the other contentions urged by learned counsel for the petitioner. 7. Suffice to note that though, the detenu was detained earlier on account of involvement in similar crime, but the said order of detention was [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
